% The aside boxes. Unnumbered, no label, and a defined term is never introduced
% inside one (\emph{..}\index{..} belongs in a definition): they are asides.
%
%   recall     -- "You already know": opens a chapter that builds on a notion
%                 owned by an earlier chapter (\cref inside the same book) or
%                 by another volume or series (named in prose, never \cref);
%                 3-5 lines. Books 1 and 2 never re-teach a notion.
%   inthefield -- "In the field": what geoscientists do outdoors. Describes
%                 professional work; the reader is never sent to a quarry, a
%                 cliff, a cave, a river in flood, or to hammer a rock.
%   inthelab   -- "In the lab": a laboratory procedure, done by professionals
%                 or with a teacher; never proposed for home.
%   history    -- a short history box: who, when, what was found.
%   dated      -- \begin{dated}{2025} ... \end{dated}: volatile figures (the
%                 latest CO2 concentration, the warmest year, a record) with
