% Map symbols. Azimuths are geographic (degrees clockwise from north); inside
% the pics TikZ angles are 90 - azimuth. One map unit = 1 cm unless the figure
% scales (then \pic[transform shape], tools/check_pic_scaling.py).
%
%   pic {northarrow}                         N arrow, 1 cm, origin at its foot
%   pic {scalebar={<cm>}{<label>}}           alternating bar, origin at left
%   pic {strikedip={<strike az>}{<dip label>}}  right-hand rule: the dip tick
%                                            points to strike + 90
%   pic {horizbed}                           horizontal bedding (circle-cross)
%   pic {vertbed={<strike az>}}              vertical bedding
%   pic {anticline={<axis az>}}, {syncline={<axis az>}}  1.6 cm fold-axis
%                                            symbol, arrows out / in
%   pic {dextral={<fault az>}}, {sinistral={<fault az>}}  half-arrows of
%                                            strike-slip sense on both sides
%
% Line styles (draw the line so that the side named below is on its LEFT,
% i.e. walk along the path with the downthrown block / overriding plate /
% advancing air on your left hand):
%   contact, unconformity (wavy), fault, normal fault (ticks on the
%   downthrown side), thrust fault (teeth on the hanging wall), ridge,
%   subduction (teeth on the overriding plate), transform,
%   cold front, warm front, occluded front (symbols on the side the front
%   moves toward), stationary front (cold symbols left, warm symbols right),
%   isobar, isotherm, contour (topographic), index contour, river.
% ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
